# Pill-Shaped Buttons

All primary site buttons must use **pill** (fully rounded) styling — not square or lightly rounded corners.

## Token

Use the shared CSS variable from `:root` in `src/assets/main.css`:

```css
--border-radius-pill: 9999px;
```

## Classes

Apply pill radius to all button/CTA classes:

- `.dev-btn`
- `.dev-btn-primary`
- `.dev-btn-outline`
- `.dev-btn-secondary`
- `.dev-apply-btn`, `.dev-apply-cta-btn`
- Header/mobile CTA links using `dev-btn` classes

```css
border-radius: var(--border-radius-pill);
```

## Do

- Use `var(--border-radius-pill)` for new buttons and CTA links
- Keep existing padding (`0.8rem 1.5rem` or similar) so pills look balanced
- Extend pill styling when adding new `.dev-btn-*` variants in `main.css`

## Don't

- Use `var(--border-radius)` (8px) or hardcoded values like `4px`, `5px`, `8px` on site CTAs
- Override pill radius in component scoped styles unless there is a strong reason

## Example

```css
/* ✅ GOOD */
.dev-btn-new {
  border-radius: var(--border-radius-pill);
}

/* ❌ BAD */
.dev-btn-new {
  border-radius: var(--border-radius);
  border-radius: 8px;
}
```
